questions.question:
A table EMPLOYEE: eid PK, name, dept, salary. Run the following and predict the output:
SELECT CONCAT(name, ' earns ', FORMAT(salary,0)) AS info FROM EMPLOYEE WHERE eid=1;
Assume row: eid=1, name='Amit', salary=75000.50

Evaluate the following query. Table EMP has columns: eid, name, dept, salary, hire_date.
SELECT dept, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE salary > 60000) AS high_earners FROM EMP GROUP BY dept;
Is this valid MySQL syntax?
